 attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLDegree.Alter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree-alter type represents the chromatic alteration for the current degree. If the degree-type value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alter or subtract, the degree-alter value is relative to the degree already in the chord based on its kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. If the degree-type value is add, the degree-alter is relative to a dominant chord (major and perfect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals except for a minor seventh). The plus-minus attribute is used to indicate if plus and minus symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. It is no if not specified."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alter"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/